<title>USA: US 9-3/4-yr indexed note sale high yield 3.650 pct.</title>
<headline>US 9-3/4-yr indexed note sale high yield 3.650 pct.</headline>
<text>
<p>WASHINGTON, April 8, Reuter - The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of inflation-indexed 9-3/4-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>		    9-3/4-YEAR NOTES DUE JAN 15, 2007</p>
<p>			   $8.003 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	3.650    Awarded At	98.307	3.375</p>
<p> MEDIAN    3.590    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 3.450    46 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.26 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 15.Jan.07</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE  9-3/4-YEAR NOTES		 PAY DATE 15.Apr.97</p>
<p>							   LAUNCHED 08.Apr.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED   8.003 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128272M3</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   18.062			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   0.04 MLN			    DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 3.375</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  0.00 MLN			 PRICE	 98.307</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    3.450-3.650 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   3.650</p>
